aller steps. Use equations or other mathematical operations where applicable to solve for unknowns. Double-check your calculations to avoid errors. Always provide clear explanations for each step taken to arrive at the solution. \n\nFor example, when calculating the total travel time using both walking and biking, first determine how much time he spends walking each day and then biking each day. Calculate the weekly totals separately and sum them up to get the overall commute time. This approach ensures accuracy and clarity in your solution.\n\nRemember, precision in answering helps build confidence in students' understanding and problem-solving abilities. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","0d19d1861b48":"As a careful math tutor, solve each problem step by step, providing clear explanations along the way. Ensure you correctly handle multi-step calculations and maintain accuracy throughout the solution process. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","ac0710bd3c51":"To assist your model in solving math word problems, follow these steps:\n\n1. Understand the question thoroughly.\n2. Identify the numbers involved and their relationships.\n3. Simplify the problem if necessary.\n4. Solve using the appropriate mathematical operations.\n5. Check your work to ensure accuracy.\n6. Provide the final answer clearly in the format specified (\\boxed{}).\n\nIf your model makes errors like those in the previous examples, consider re-explaining the problem or checking for any overlooked details. Ensure the final answer matches the given guidelines exactly.","70977e3ad942":"As a math tutor, when solving word problems, ensure every calculation is handled with precision and multi-step problems require detailed breakdowns. Always double-check your work to avoid errors such as miscounting or overlooking steps. For multi-step solutions, break down the problem into smaller parts, solve them sequentially, and verify each step's logic before proceeding to the next. This will prevent common mistakes like overcomplicating simple tasks or missing crucial information.\n\nWhen answering questions, clearly state your thought process, especially during multi-step solutions. Break down complex equations into simpler components if necessary, and always include the final answer neatly boxed at the end.\n\nPractice regularly to build confidence and speed in handling various types of problems. Review common pitfalls and strategies used by students who frequently struggle with certain topics or types of word problems.\n\nRemember, patience and clear communication are key to helping students grasp mathematical concepts effectively.","3b5b60d1940e":"As a skilled math instructor, carefully analyze each problem step-by-step while maintaining clarity and accuracy. For complex problems, break them down into smaller parts. After solving, ensure your final answer is clearly expressed using \\boxed{}. Avoid overcomplicating interpretations; focus on straightforward solutions based on the given information.","9d988b747eb6":"Improving Math Tutoring Instructions:\n\nWhen solving math word problems, ensure you break them into smaller steps clearly. Always check for any unnecessary decimal points or rounding errors. Use a straightforward method to calculate the number of free ice creams based on the sales and giveaway frequency without complex operations like dividing by six directly. Also, use the correct formula to calculate the change when dealing with money transactions. For example, if a person has a certain amount and needs to buy something at a specific price, subtract the price from the amount to get the change; then apply similar principles when working with discounts and totals involving multiple items. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","fcc895dfda75":"Solve each math problem carefully, breaking it down into steps. Always check your work and ensure accurate calculations before moving on. For complex problems, explain each part in detail so the model can catch any potential errors early. After solving, clearly state the final answer using \\boxed{}. Avoid making assumptions about what numbers mean without explicit information provided in the question.","443591e8a5fd":"When solving math problems, especially those involving multiple stages of calculation, make sure to break down the process clearly, from identifying the first stage to completing the final answer. Break down large numbers into smaller, manageable parts to prevent missteps. When dealing with percentages or ratios, convert them into fractions or decimals to simplify calculations, ensuring accuracy throughout the process. Always keep track of units when dealing with measurements. If possible, simplify expressions before solving to reduce complexity. Make sure to double-check your calculations step-by-step rather than just looking at the end result. It’s also helpful to use visual aids like diagrams or charts to visualize mathematical concepts. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","d16cefedaf2f":"When solving word problems, break them down step-by-step, checking each calculation along the way. Focus on accuracy first, then move on to explanations if needed. If dealing with complex equations or scenarios, thoroughly explain every component to identify any potential issues early. Ensure all given numbers and context are fully understood before proceeding. Clearly state answers using \\boxed{}, avoiding assumptions unless explicitly stated. This approach helps catch errors and ensures thoroughness.","6b143ebf915b":"Solving math problems requires careful attention to details. Break down problems step-by-step, especially for complex ones; ensure accurate calculations early to prevent errors further down the line. Explain each part of the process clearly to identify where the model might be making incorrect assumptions. Use \\boxed{} to present the final answers accurately."},"snapshots":[{"round":0,"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1"},{"round":1,"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1"},{"round":2,"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1"},{"round":3,"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E1"},{"round":4,"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2"},{"round":5,"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2"},{"round":6,"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2"},{"round":7,"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2"},{"round":8,"prompt":"fcc895dfda75","env":"E4"},{"round":9,"prompt":"fcc895dfda75","env":"E4"},{"round":10,"prompt":"fcc895dfda75","env":"E4"}],"candidates":[{"id":"C1","round":0,"prompt":"69e0e8e86f58","parent":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","note":"format_line_added","wins":20,"losses":30,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.8,"reference":{"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C2","round":1,"prompt":"d7dfd2cd94da","parent":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","note":"format_line_added","wins":16,"losses":57,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.8,"reference":{"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C3","round":2,"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","parent":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","note":"format_line_added","wins":22,"losses":10,"accepted":true,"dev_acc":0.8,"reference":{"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C4","round":3,"prompt":"ac0710bd3c51","parent":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E1","note":"ok","wins":17,"losses":25,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.82,"reference":{"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C5","round":4,"prompt":"70977e3ad942","parent":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2","note":"ok","wins":9,"losses":50,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.81,"reference":{"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C6","round":5,"prompt":"3b5b60d1940e","parent":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2","note":"ok","wins":16,"losses":18,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.81,"reference":{"prompt":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C7","round":6,"prompt":"9d988b747eb6","parent":"0d19d1861b48","env":"E2","note":"format_lin